    <span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</span>
    <h1>Hanoi Motorbike Rental: Backpackers Pickup Planning</h1>
    <p>Pickup day is the hinge of a backpacker's month in Hanoi: the day the trip stops being a plan and starts being a machine in your hands. Planning it well means arriving at the shop at the right hour, with the right things in your pockets, asking the right questions at the counter, and riding away on a bike whose paperwork, condition and controls you already understand. This guide walks the whole pickup sequence for the backpacker profile, from timing the visit to the first kilometer home, without promising anything the shop has not verified itself.</p>
    <p>The page belongs to the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> cluster, written for backpackers. The verified fleet prices live on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">cost hub</a>, the general question bank is on the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> page, and the questions to ask at the counter are collected in the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/backpackers-rental-paperwork-questions/">rental paperwork guide</a> for the same audience.</p>

    <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
      <p>On this page</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#sec-1">Why pickup day deserves a plan</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-2">Getting to the Long Bien shop</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-3">Timing: the hours that make pickup easy</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-4">What to bring and what to ask</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-5">The handover: photos, fuel and controls</a></li>
